cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  FEM@ti — Elastic–plastic Timoshenko beam finite element analysis
message: >-
  If you use this software in academic work, please cite it using the
  metadata below. Note that the underlying mechanical model originates
  from the author's 1996 MSc thesis, referenced separately.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bánya
    given-names: Attila
    affiliation: >-
      Faktum Invest Kft. — formerly Budapest University of Technology
      and Economics (BME), Faculty of Civil Engineering
repository-code: 'https://github.com/banyaattila-crypto/FEMAti'
url: 'https://femati.vercel.app'
abstract: >-
  A browser-based, dependency-light finite element program for
  elastic–plastic analysis of Timoshenko beams. It reimplements the
  numerical apparatus of a 1996 BME MSc thesis — 3-node quadratic
  isoparametric beam elements, selective reduced integration against
  shear locking, a layered (fiber) cross-section model and a
  Newton–Raphson elastic–plastic solver — with line-by-line
  traceability from code to the original derivation, and a closed-form
  validation suite. The original frontal equation solver is preserved
  as an animated "historical mode" alongside the modern skyline solver.
  This is research and educational software, not certified design
  software.
keywords:
  - finite element method
  - Timoshenko beam
  - elastic-plastic analysis
  - structural engineering
  - Eurocode
  - TypeScript
